Package: xenon-xws
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         winehq-stable | wine (>= 10),
         zenity,
         libnotify-bin,
         xdg-user-dirs,
         e2fsprogs,
         x11-xserver-utils,
         cabextract,
         unzip,
         p7zip-full,
         curl
Recommends: xenon-xws-thirdparty,
            gamemode,
            mangohud,
            vulkan-tools,
            desktop-file-utils,
            fonts-liberation2,
            fonts-crosextra-carlito,
            fonts-crosextra-caladea,
            fonts-noto-core,
            fonts-dejavu-core
Description: Xenon Windows Subsystem
 Runs Windows programs as a built-in part of Xenon. XWS manages one
 Windows environment per user on top of Wine, maps drives and user
 folders, turns Start Menu shortcuts into app grid entries, installs
 runtimes (Visual C++, DirectX extras, .NET) on demand, applies per-app
 compatibility profiles and keeps registry snapshots. Double-clicking a
 Windows installer (exe or msi) just works, and binfmt_misc lets Windows
 programs run from a terminal.

Package: xenon-branding
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         plymouth,
         plymouth-label
Description: Xenon artwork and identity
 Logo, icons, wallpapers, boot splash (Plymouth), boot menu (GRUB) and
 login screen branding for Xenon, plus the operating system release
 information (/usr/lib/os-release).

Package: xenon-system
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         systemd-zram-generator,
         ufw,
         unattended-upgrades,
         flatpak
Recommends: gamemode
Description: Xenon system defaults and tuning
 Gaming and desktop tuning (vm.max_map_count, split-lock handling, zram
 swap), low-latency PipeWire audio for games and music production,
 controller permissions, privacy-respecting GNOME and Firefox defaults,
 automatic security updates, firewall on by default, and APT pinning for
 the newer kernel, Mesa and NVIDIA packages from Debian backports.

Package: xenon-settings
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
         pkexec,
         pciutils,
         mokutil,
         ufw,
         xenon-xws
Description: Xenon Settings and Welcome
 Manage installed Windows apps, Windows compatibility, graphics drivers
 (including NVIDIA), privacy, firewall and updates. Includes the
 first-boot Welcome app with a hardware check.

Package: xenon-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         calamares,
         xenon-branding,
         x11-xserver-utils,
         sudo,
         os-prober,
         efibootmgr,
         cryptsetup,
         cryptsetup-initramfs
Description: Xenon installer configuration (live session only)
 Calamares configuration, branding and helper scripts used by the Xenon
 live ISO to install Xenon. Removed automatically from installed systems.

Package: xenon-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         xenon-xws,
         xenon-branding,
         xenon-system,
         xenon-settings,
         gnome-core,
         gnome-software,
         gnome-software-plugin-flatpak,
         gnome-shell-extension-dashtodock,
         gnome-shell-extension-appindicator,
         pipewire-audio,
         network-manager,
         fwupd
Recommends: xenon-xws-thirdparty,
            firefox-esr,
            switcheroo-control,
            power-profiles-daemon
Description: Xenon desktop (metapackage)
 Installs the complete Xenon desktop on top of Debian: GNOME, the Xenon
 Windows Subsystem, settings, branding and system defaults.
